WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.282 --> 00:00:02.531
- Good morning Believe Nation,
my name is Evan Carmichael,

00:00:02.531 --> 00:00:04.127
my one word is believe.

00:00:04.127 --> 00:00:06.527
And I believe that
entrepreneurs will solve all of

00:00:06.527 --> 00:00:08.256
the world's major problems.

00:00:08.256 --> 00:00:10.940
So to help you on your
journey, today's message is:

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:12.432
take action.

00:00:12.432 --> 00:00:14.306
Over to you Mel Robbins.

00:00:14.306 --> 00:00:16.687
(rooster crows)

00:00:16.687 --> 00:00:19.271
- ♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:19.271 --> 00:00:22.159
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:00:22.159 --> 00:00:26.328
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:26.328 --> 00:00:28.684
- One night, Chris had gone to bed.

00:00:28.684 --> 00:00:30.459
I had been struggling,
struggling, struggling.

00:00:30.459 --> 00:00:32.899
We still had all the same problems.

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:34.531
I, we still had a lien on the house,

00:00:34.531 --> 00:00:36.837
still facing bankruptcy,
still fighting like crazy,

00:00:36.837 --> 00:00:38.754
I was still unemployed.

00:00:39.753 --> 00:00:41.854
He still, they still
hadn't figured out, like,

00:00:41.854 --> 00:00:44.675
the solution yet for the business.

00:00:44.675 --> 00:00:48.683
And I was about to turn off
the TV, and there on the TV

00:00:48.683 --> 00:00:50.508
there was this rocket
launching, and I thought,

00:00:50.508 --> 00:00:52.425
Oh my gosh, that is it!

00:00:55.686 --> 00:01:00.172
I am going to launch myself
out of bed like a rocket ship,

00:01:00.172 --> 00:01:03.760
like NASA, right here, had
launched me out of that bed.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:06.918
And I am going to move so
fast that I don't think.

00:01:06.918 --> 00:01:09.076
- Mm.
- I'm going to beat my brain.

00:01:09.076 --> 00:01:12.326
Now here is a really interesting point.

00:01:13.632 --> 00:01:17.836
I talk a lot about your
instincts and inner wisdom,

00:01:17.836 --> 00:01:20.279
and we can get into
this a little bit later,

00:01:20.279 --> 00:01:21.890
but a lot of us talk about
the fact that you have

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:22.806
a gut feeling.

00:01:22.806 --> 00:01:25.870
But what all this research
that I've done for the book,

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:28.100
and all the speaking that
I do, what I've discovered

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:31.012
that's fascinating is
actually, when you set goals,

00:01:31.012 --> 00:01:32.712
when you have an intention on something

00:01:32.712 --> 00:01:34.669
that you want to change about your life,

00:01:34.669 --> 00:01:36.145
your brain helps you.

00:01:36.145 --> 00:01:38.741
What it does is it opens up a checklist

00:01:38.741 --> 00:01:42.219
and then your brain goes to
work trying to remind you

00:01:42.219 --> 00:01:43.052
- Yeah.

00:01:43.052 --> 00:01:45.105
- of that intention that you set.

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:48.485
And it's really important
to develop the skill.

00:01:48.485 --> 00:01:51.142
And I say that word
purposefully, the skill

00:01:51.142 --> 00:01:53.774
of knowing how to hear that inner wisdom

00:01:53.774 --> 00:01:56.061
and that intention kicking in.

00:01:56.061 --> 00:01:58.233
And leaning into it quickly.
- Mmm.

00:01:58.233 --> 00:02:01.566
- So for me, my brain saying,
that's it, right there.

00:02:01.566 --> 00:02:03.962
Move as fast as a rocket, Mel.

00:02:03.962 --> 00:02:07.103
I wanted to change my life,
and I think most people

00:02:07.103 --> 00:02:10.573
that are miserable, or
that are really, like,

00:02:10.573 --> 00:02:12.783
dying to be great,
- Mmm.

00:02:12.783 --> 00:02:14.899
- and dying to have
more, we want to change,

00:02:14.899 --> 00:02:18.193
we want to live a better
life, we want to create more

00:02:18.193 --> 00:02:20.921
for our families, we want to be happier.

00:02:20.921 --> 00:02:23.418
The desire is there.

00:02:23.418 --> 00:02:25.827
Again, it's about how do you
go from knowledge to action?

00:02:25.827 --> 00:02:28.152
So the first thing in this
story that's important

00:02:28.152 --> 00:02:31.688
is realizing that the answer
was in me, and my mind

00:02:31.688 --> 00:02:34.323
was telling me, pay attention.

00:02:34.323 --> 00:02:35.377
It could have also been the bourbon.

00:02:35.377 --> 00:02:36.210
(laughs)
I mean I had a couple

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:38.530
Manhattans that night, but.

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:41.236
Anyway, the next morning,
the alarm goes off

00:02:41.236 --> 00:02:43.819
and I pretended NASA was there.

00:02:45.623 --> 00:02:46.590
It's the stupidest story.

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:49.078
I literally went five,
four, three, two, one.

00:02:49.078 --> 00:02:52.160
I counted out loud, and then I stood up.

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:55.125
And I'll never forget
standing there in my bedroom.

00:02:55.125 --> 00:02:59.937
It was dark, it was cold,
it was winter in Boston.

00:02:59.937 --> 00:03:01.121
- Mm-hmm.

00:03:01.121 --> 00:03:03.430
- And for the first time in three months,

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:08.087
I had beaten my habit of
hitting the snooze button.

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:11.131
I couldn't believe it, and
I thought, wait a minute.

00:03:11.131 --> 00:03:13.130
Counting backwards, that
is the dumbest thing

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:15.191
I've ever heard of in my entire life.

00:03:15.191 --> 00:03:17.341
Well the next morning I used
it again, and it worked.

00:03:17.341 --> 00:03:19.119
The next morning I used
it again, and it worked.

00:03:19.119 --> 00:03:21.480
The next morning I used
it again, and it worked.

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:24.852
And then I started to notice
something really interesting.

00:03:24.852 --> 00:03:28.685
There were moments all
day long, all day long,

00:03:29.699 --> 00:03:33.849
just like that five second moment in bed,

00:03:33.849 --> 00:03:37.349
where I knew, knowledge, what I should do.

00:03:38.925 --> 00:03:42.071
And if I didn't move within five seconds,

00:03:42.071 --> 00:03:44.109
my brain would step in
and talk me out of it.

00:03:44.109 --> 00:03:45.188
- Mm.

00:03:45.188 --> 00:03:47.310
- Every human being has
a five second window.

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:50.370
Might even be shorter for you.

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:52.943
You have about a five
second window in which

00:03:52.943 --> 00:03:56.699
you can move from idea to
action before your brain

00:03:56.699 --> 00:04:00.866
kicks into full gear and
sabotages any change in behavior.

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:04.995
Cause remember, your brain
is wired to stop you from

00:04:04.995 --> 00:04:06.945
doing things that are
uncomfortable, or uncertain,

00:04:06.945 --> 00:04:07.778
or scary.

00:04:08.842 --> 00:04:12.786
It's your job to learn how
to move from those ideas

00:04:12.786 --> 00:04:16.509
that could change everything,
into acting on them.

00:04:16.509 --> 00:04:18.025
- Taking action is a cure-all.

00:04:18.025 --> 00:04:20.549
Taking action solves all the problems that

00:04:20.549 --> 00:04:21.717
you're going through.

00:04:21.717 --> 00:04:23.211
Whatever problem you have, whatever thing

00:04:23.211 --> 00:04:25.608
is in front of you,
whatever obstacle is there

00:04:25.608 --> 00:04:28.482
that seems usurmountable,
it's not going to get fixed

00:04:28.482 --> 00:04:31.294
by just sitting and
complaining and wallowing,

00:04:31.294 --> 00:04:32.847
and feeling sorry for yourself.

00:04:32.847 --> 00:04:35.251
It happens from taking action.

00:04:35.251 --> 00:04:36.958
As soon as you can move from that place

00:04:36.958 --> 00:04:41.699
of being unhappy and desperate,
and sorry for yourself

00:04:41.699 --> 00:04:44.302
to how do I solve this?

00:04:44.302 --> 00:04:46.158
Who do I need to contact to help me?

00:04:46.158 --> 00:04:48.881
How can I use the resources
I have to fix this?

00:04:48.881 --> 00:04:50.630
As soon as you start moving to that land,

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:52.655
that's when you start to make progress.

00:04:52.655 --> 00:04:54.736
Taking action is the cure-all.

00:04:54.736 --> 00:04:57.374
This is what happens so
many times to entrepreneurs,

00:04:57.374 --> 00:05:00.069
not even just with problems,
but with ideas in general.

00:05:00.069 --> 00:05:01.687
How often do you get an idea for something

00:05:01.687 --> 00:05:04.166
that you want to do, and
then you say, tomorrow

00:05:04.166 --> 00:05:05.659
I'm going to do it?

00:05:05.659 --> 00:05:07.632
And then tomorrow comes, you don't do it.

00:05:07.632 --> 00:05:08.465
How many times?

00:05:08.465 --> 00:05:10.815
That happens, that happens
over and over and over and over

00:05:10.815 --> 00:05:12.289
and again. It's a human condition.

00:05:12.289 --> 00:05:13.519
It's not just entrepreneurs.

00:05:13.519 --> 00:05:15.681
We have these things, these
ambitions, these drives

00:05:15.681 --> 00:05:17.058
that we set for ourselves
and then we don't

00:05:17.058 --> 00:05:18.359
follow through on.

00:05:18.359 --> 00:05:22.058
The best way to start
on that idea you have

00:05:22.058 --> 00:05:23.278
is to take action.

00:05:23.278 --> 00:05:24.615
Do something immediately.

00:05:24.615 --> 00:05:27.367
As soon as you set a goal, I
want to start a YouTube channel.

00:05:27.367 --> 00:05:28.200
Great.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:29.178
What are you going to
do on You Tube channel?

00:05:29.178 --> 00:05:30.388
I want to interview people.

00:05:30.388 --> 00:05:31.850
Amazing.

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:34.581
Today, set up your YouTube
channel and send out

00:05:34.581 --> 00:05:37.355
ten emails to people to
ask them for interviews.

00:05:37.355 --> 00:05:39.722
People that you know, people
who you think will say yes.

00:05:39.722 --> 00:05:41.560
When you commit to somebody
else, you're much more

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:42.837
likely to follow through.

00:05:42.837 --> 00:05:47.705
And what happens is perfection
becomes the enemy of action.

00:05:47.705 --> 00:05:50.975
You want to make it perfect,
and because you make it perfect

00:05:50.975 --> 00:05:53.812
it gets more and more and
more and more complex,

00:05:53.812 --> 00:05:57.703
and complexion is the enemy of execution.

00:05:57.703 --> 00:06:00.167
Because you build it up
to be this big thing,

00:06:00.167 --> 00:06:02.137
this big scary thing
that has to be perfect.

00:06:02.137 --> 00:06:03.668
You don't do anything.

00:06:03.668 --> 00:06:05.664
Before I set up my YouTube
channel I need to have

00:06:05.664 --> 00:06:07.398
the perfect channel
art, and I need to have

00:06:07.398 --> 00:06:09.343
the right thumbnails, and I
need to know what my script

00:06:09.343 --> 00:06:11.808
is going to be, and I need
to know my intro and opener,

00:06:11.808 --> 00:06:12.921
and I need the gear.

00:06:12.921 --> 00:06:14.454
All of these things that
you need to have to make

00:06:14.454 --> 00:06:15.851
a perfect video.

00:06:15.851 --> 00:06:17.608
And because it becomes this big thing,

00:06:17.608 --> 00:06:19.492
you don't do anything about it.

00:06:19.492 --> 00:06:21.348
And then the next day you
wake up, and it's gone.

00:06:21.348 --> 00:06:22.630
Poof.

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:26.284
As soon as you set a goal for yourself,

00:06:26.284 --> 00:06:28.367
I want to go and do this,

00:06:29.954 --> 00:06:32.808
the best next thing
you can do is take some

00:06:32.808 --> 00:06:35.891
form of immediate action and ideally,

00:06:37.267 --> 00:06:39.376
commit to somebody else.

00:06:39.376 --> 00:06:42.056
Whether it's a friend, whether
it's a potential customer,

00:06:42.056 --> 00:06:45.358
whether you're sending emails
out, whether it's your family,

00:06:45.358 --> 00:06:49.192
whether it's a neighbor,
commit to somebody else.

00:06:49.192 --> 00:06:51.511
Because when you do that,
you're much more likely

00:06:51.511 --> 00:06:53.797
to follow through because
you won't let them down.

00:06:53.797 --> 00:06:56.105
You'll let yourself down all the time.

00:06:56.105 --> 00:06:57.716
You'll let yourself down
every morning when you wake up

00:06:57.716 --> 00:06:58.885
and hit the snooze button.

00:06:58.885 --> 00:06:59.718
You're letting yourself down.

00:06:59.718 --> 00:07:02.517
The first thing you do in the
morning is let yourself down.

00:07:02.517 --> 00:07:03.350
You set a goal,

00:07:03.350 --> 00:07:04.724
Boom. I let myself down.

00:07:04.724 --> 00:07:06.744
You let yourself down all the time.

00:07:06.744 --> 00:07:09.427
But you won't let other
people down nearly as much.

00:07:09.427 --> 00:07:13.680
So take immediate action,
and then follow through

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:17.011
with somebody else so that
you don't let yourself,

00:07:17.011 --> 00:07:18.423
and them down.

00:07:18.423 --> 00:07:19.625
So the question of the day today is,

00:07:19.625 --> 00:07:21.188
I'm curious, what is one big

00:07:21.188 --> 00:07:23.655
goal you have, and one action
that you're going to take

00:07:23.655 --> 00:07:27.137
today, not tomorrow, right
now, right after posting

00:07:27.137 --> 00:07:30.381
this comment, you're going to
go take action, immediately?

00:07:30.381 --> 00:07:31.342
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:07:31.342 --> 00:07:32.667
Really curious to find out.

00:07:32.667 --> 00:07:34.468
I also want to give a
quick shout out to Julia

00:07:34.468 --> 00:07:36.276
from insidethejewelbox.com.

00:07:36.276 --> 00:07:38.932
Julia, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:07:38.932 --> 00:07:40.044
Your One Word.

00:07:40.044 --> 00:07:41.705
I really, really, really
appreciate the support,

00:07:41.705 --> 00:07:43.435
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:07:43.435 --> 00:07:44.810
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:45.977
I believe in you.

00:07:45.977 --> 00:07:48.048
I hope you continue to believe in yourelf,

00:07:48.048 --> 00:07:50.071
and whatever your one word is.

00:07:50.071 --> 00:07:52.508
Much love and I'll see you
guys again tomorrow morning

00:07:52.508 --> 00:07:55.284
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:07:55.284 --> 00:07:57.841
- ♫ I wake up every morning

00:07:57.841 --> 00:08:01.424
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:08:03.856 --> 00:08:05.459
- Take action.

00:08:05.459 --> 00:08:08.535
Whatever you want to do, whatever
you're thinking about it,

00:08:08.535 --> 00:08:13.077
you will not get it until you
take action, make that move.

00:08:13.077 --> 00:08:14.222
Make it a small step.

00:08:14.222 --> 00:08:16.919
If you want a house, go get a rug.

00:08:16.919 --> 00:08:17.752
You know what I mean?

00:08:17.752 --> 00:08:20.479
If you want a new car, go
get some car freshener.

00:08:20.479 --> 00:08:23.446
Take action. Make this
thing happen for you,

00:08:23.446 --> 00:08:25.359
and it will happen.

00:08:25.359 --> 00:08:27.958
Action, action, action.

00:08:27.958 --> 00:08:31.775
You know one thing that
I can really attribute

00:08:31.775 --> 00:08:35.942
to every failure in my life,
whether it be personal,

00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:42.857
financial, any kind of
way, business, whatever,

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:49.692
it's because of a lack of
my attempt to take action.

00:08:49.692 --> 00:08:52.205
I did not take action.

00:08:52.205 --> 00:08:56.038
And, it kind of changed
once I got the fact that

00:08:57.137 --> 00:08:58.637
action is the key.

00:08:59.699 --> 00:09:00.692
It changed my life.

00:09:00.692 --> 00:09:04.036
- You have to actually show up every day

00:09:04.036 --> 00:09:08.100
and inch yourself forward
toward these dreams.

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:10.730
And not only show up every
day and once in a while

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:14.065
inch yourself, I mean every
day, you have to actually

00:09:14.065 --> 00:09:16.359
take an action that moves you forward.

00:09:16.359 --> 00:09:18.566
Not just research, not just thinking.

00:09:18.566 --> 00:09:21.002
Look, the power of the intention is great,

00:09:21.002 --> 00:09:24.006
but without any initiative
it's dead, right.

00:09:24.006 --> 00:09:28.054
A dream is great, but without
any movement, it's dead.

00:09:28.054 --> 00:09:31.020
You have to be moving
towards it every day.

00:09:31.020 --> 00:09:33.200
You can send an email every
day, you can make a call

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:35.502
every day, you can write
something every day,

00:09:35.502 --> 00:09:37.137
you can create something
everyday, you can contribute

00:09:37.137 --> 00:09:40.258
something every day,
but it has to be daily.

00:09:40.258 --> 00:09:43.586
Otherwise it will never become actualized.

00:09:43.586 --> 00:09:45.243
The highest performers in
the world didn't get there

00:09:45.243 --> 00:09:46.418
cause they were lucky.

00:09:46.418 --> 00:09:48.819
They worked at it longer
than everyone else.

00:09:48.819 --> 00:09:51.106
They had a better work
ethic, and it's not that they

00:09:51.106 --> 00:09:52.953
necessarily always worked harder.

00:09:52.953 --> 00:09:56.234
They worked smarter because
they were doing the research,

00:09:56.234 --> 00:09:58.452
they were taking the time
to visualize how they

00:09:58.452 --> 00:10:01.435
would be distinct, different,
how they would survive

00:10:01.435 --> 00:10:02.358
the tough times.

00:10:02.358 --> 00:10:04.319
They really kept at it.

00:10:04.319 --> 00:10:07.986
Keep every single day
momentum going, and if

00:10:08.923 --> 00:10:10.678
you don't do that, there's no chance.

00:10:10.678 --> 00:10:14.308
- One of the functions of
belief is taking action.

00:10:14.308 --> 00:10:17.193
We did a survey of about
2000 top entrepreneurs,

00:10:17.193 --> 00:10:19.187
and we noticed that one
of the things that people

00:10:19.187 --> 00:10:21.937
who win in that world
have is a bias for action.

00:10:21.937 --> 00:10:24.617
If they have an
inspiration, they act on it.

00:10:24.617 --> 00:10:26.299
How many of you have
ever had a great idea,

00:10:26.299 --> 00:10:28.498
talked about it, thought
about it, didn't do it.

00:10:28.498 --> 00:10:30.528
Then someone else did
it and was successful,

00:10:30.528 --> 00:10:32.327
and you went, darn, I
should have done that?

00:10:32.327 --> 00:10:34.075
Maybe it was buy that piece of property.

00:10:34.075 --> 00:10:35.605
You notice we all have
that piece of property

00:10:35.605 --> 00:10:36.788
we wish we'd bought?

00:10:36.788 --> 00:10:38.113
You know.

00:10:38.113 --> 00:10:40.589
Anyway, so we're going
to be looking at the idea

00:10:40.589 --> 00:10:43.240
that taking action is
part of law of attraction.

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:45.305
See, a lot of people think
you just sit in your room,

00:10:45.305 --> 00:10:47.627
meditate, visualize
having the perfect car,

00:10:47.627 --> 00:10:49.889
the perfect house, the
perfect relationship,

00:10:49.889 --> 00:10:51.795
then it'll kind of just come to you.

00:10:51.795 --> 00:10:54.393
And I always say, unless you
live at the bottom of a hill,

00:10:54.393 --> 00:10:55.885
(laughter

00:10:55.885 --> 00:10:58.249
where there's a road, there's
probably not going to be

00:10:58.249 --> 00:10:59.677
a Cadillac showing up in your living room,

00:10:59.677 --> 00:11:01.150
(laughter)
right.

00:11:01.150 --> 00:11:04.591
So, think about this, the
last six letters of the word,

00:11:04.591 --> 00:11:06.213
attraction, spell what?

00:11:06.213 --> 00:11:08.676
- Action.
- A-C-T-I-O-N, action.

00:11:08.676 --> 00:11:11.240
Now there's two kinds of
actions that are critical.

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:12.692
There's obvious actions.

00:11:12.692 --> 00:11:14.553
If you want a certain kind
of car, you should go down

00:11:14.553 --> 00:11:15.713
and test drive it.

00:11:15.713 --> 00:11:17.455
You should find out how much it costs.

00:11:17.455 --> 00:11:20.099
You should see what it
costs to maintain it.

00:11:20.099 --> 00:11:23.058
You should go, you know, spend,
I like to test drive a car

00:11:23.058 --> 00:11:25.520
three or four times, go down
to the dealer, take a camera,

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:27.295
stick my head out the window
and say, take a picture of me,

00:11:27.295 --> 00:11:29.779
I'll be back to buy it.
(laughter)

00:11:29.779 --> 00:11:32.975
Put it up on my refrigerator,
look at it every day.

00:11:32.975 --> 00:11:36.178
Eventually, you know, those kind
of things produce car, right,

00:11:36.178 --> 00:11:37.580
saving for it and so forth.

00:11:37.580 --> 00:11:40.539
But there are also things
called inspired actions.

00:11:40.539 --> 00:11:43.301
All of a sudden, you get an
inspiration to do something,

00:11:43.301 --> 00:11:45.318
and you didn't know what it was.

00:11:45.318 --> 00:11:47.293
You don't have the sense of
like, how's this rationally

00:11:47.293 --> 00:11:50.276
going to make sense for me
to move forward in my life?

00:11:50.276 --> 00:11:51.204
I'll give you an example.

00:11:51.204 --> 00:11:54.054
A friend if mine, Dr.
Ignatius Piazza, graduates

00:11:54.054 --> 00:11:55.377
chiropractic school.

00:11:55.377 --> 00:11:57.720
He wants to move to
Monterey, near Pebble Beach,

00:11:57.720 --> 00:11:59.074
where the golf course is.

00:11:59.074 --> 00:12:00.453
And he gets there and he says to the local

00:12:00.453 --> 00:12:02.912
Chiropractic Association,
like to join you,

00:12:02.912 --> 00:12:04.420
I'd like you to help me
get my practice started,

00:12:04.420 --> 00:12:06.339
and they said, we don't
need any more chiropractors.

00:12:06.339 --> 00:12:08.750
We have one chiropractor
for every eight people

00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:10.766
in this area; there's too many.

00:12:10.766 --> 00:12:13.650
Now he could've said, okay, let
the external reality control

00:12:13.650 --> 00:12:16.181
his internal experience,
but he didn't do that.

00:12:16.181 --> 00:12:19.514
He said I'm going to think
about this, and visualize it,

00:12:19.514 --> 00:12:22.173
and believe in it, and something
will come that I will do.

00:12:22.173 --> 00:12:24.913
And what came to him to
do was to take six months

00:12:24.913 --> 00:12:27.482
before he opened his
office, and put a pin where

00:12:27.482 --> 00:12:30.106
he wanted his office and
in concentric circles,

00:12:30.106 --> 00:12:32.319
knock on every door in
every neighborhood, saying,

00:12:32.319 --> 00:12:34.080
Hi, I'm a new doctor
in town, can I ask you

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:35.495
a few questions?

00:12:35.495 --> 00:12:36.886
You know, I'm starting
this practice, should I

00:12:36.886 --> 00:12:40.473
open from five til nine in the
morning, or should I be open

00:12:40.473 --> 00:12:42.737
from five until nine at
night for people who have

00:12:42.737 --> 00:12:43.570
nine to five jobs?

00:12:43.570 --> 00:12:44.499
Which would be better?

00:12:44.499 --> 00:12:46.651
Should I advertise in
this paper, or that paper?

00:12:46.651 --> 00:12:48.771
Should I call it Ignatius
Piazza Chiropractic,

00:12:48.771 --> 00:12:50.588
or Chiropractic West?

00:12:50.588 --> 00:12:52.362
And then his last question
was, if I have an open house,

00:12:52.362 --> 00:12:54.609
would you like to receive an invitation?

00:12:54.609 --> 00:12:56.248
They said yes, he wrote it down.

00:12:56.248 --> 00:13:00.043
Now over six months, he
knocked on 12,500 doors,

00:13:00.043 --> 00:13:04.148
talked to 6,500 people, and
gathered over 4,000 names

00:13:04.148 --> 00:13:06.099
of people who said, yes,
I'd like an invitation

00:13:06.099 --> 00:13:07.635
to your open house.

00:13:07.635 --> 00:13:09.719
Now, when he opened his
office six months later

00:13:09.719 --> 00:13:11.931
in a town that did not
need another chiropractor,

00:13:11.931 --> 00:13:15.011
according to the professionals,
his first month in practice

00:13:15.011 --> 00:13:16.939
he netted $72,000.

00:13:16.939 --> 00:13:18.656
(gasps)

00:13:18.656 --> 00:13:20.657
In his first year in
practice, his gross income

00:13:20.657 --> 00:13:23.210
was over a million dollars.

00:13:23.210 --> 00:13:25.219
I was giving a talk and
mentioned this story

00:13:25.219 --> 00:13:26.798
just about five years
ago, and this happened

00:13:26.798 --> 00:13:29.080
about 25 years ago.

00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:30.955
Someone said, he knocked on my door.

00:13:30.955 --> 00:13:33.205
(laughter)

00:13:34.145 --> 00:13:35.851
And he left his card.

00:13:35.851 --> 00:13:37.553
And two years later, I
needed a chiropractor,

00:13:37.553 --> 00:13:38.410
and I called him.

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:40.311
Because we work with
people we know, we've had

00:13:40.311 --> 00:13:41.474
an experience with, right.

00:13:41.474 --> 00:13:44.309
So he trusted his intuition,
he took action on it.

00:13:44.309 --> 00:13:47.905
Other people would say, uh,
guess I can't have what I want.

00:13:47.905 --> 00:13:49.552
You got to be willing to take the action.

